 — the four lean tasks, `cells` and `load`: fields, refusals by status `1`, usage by `2`, session errors by `3`; since 2026-10-20-large-screen-in-parts `snapshot --part` read by number answering one uncoloured JSON line, status 0, and `--part` 0, 1001 and `x` exiting 1 with a line equal to `Refusal::malformed(fault).to_json()`, nothing typed written back; since 2026-10-31-select-popup `a_hosted_click_opens_a_list_a_shot_shows_it_and_a_click_on_a_row_chooses`, in `cc-popup`, the hosted shot equal to the in-process one; since 2026-11-07-ui-graph `graph_answers_one_line_of_the_ui_graph`, `graph` run as a process answering one line of the UI graph, status 0, an argument to it refused `malformed`, status 1; since 2026-11-08-what-can-i-do-here `actions_answers_one_line_of_the_actionable_nodes`, `actions` run as a process against a started host answering one JSON line, an argument to it refused, status 1; since 2026-11-08-handler-coverage `coverage_replays_a_kept_check_and_lists_the_handlers_it_left`, the binary's `coverage` role over a Counter check the binary kept answering the handlers it left in one coverage line on stdout, status 0) and `cli_flow` (two POSIX `sh` flows, `counter.sh` and `flight.sh`); since 2026-10-19-session-recording `recording` (4 tests, unix only, and 1 off-unix; 3 until 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay: the command line and the `mcp` role keep the same check byte for byte, the state directory gone after `stop`; a recording directory open to its group refused before anything runs; the `mcp` role's listing and `help` the same with and without `--record`; since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay the committed checks what the binary records, `examples/seven_guis/tests/flows/record_checks.sh` run through the binary and both files compared byte for byte with the committed copies; off unix, `--record` refused `Unsupported`); since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `mcp_server` (the `mcp` role completes the Counter flow by tool calls alone; a `lint` tool call answering its line of findings; a `graph` tool call answering its line of the UI graph; an `actions` tool call answering its line of the actionable nodes, an argument to it reading `isError`; protocol errors run nothing and leak nothing; unix only, a snapshot equal through MCP and the command line) and `mcp_log` (the role at `RUST_LOG=trace`: no id, name or typed text, one `tool_call` line per call, under both builds; twelve tool calls and 10 `command` lines, one `lint`, one `snapshot` part read, one `graph` call and one `actions` call among them, 0 graph and 0 actions needles read; since 2026-10-19-session-recording a second test, a recording `mcp` role that logs nothing of its checks; and a third, a select list opened and chosen through the role, `a_select_list_opened_and_chosen_through_the_role_logs_no_option_at_trace`, which records nothing — 0 option needles at `trace`), not unix-gated but the comparison and, since that chunk, every check that records (`mcp_log`'s recorded test, the shared `common::recorded_needles` (its own until 2026-10-19-test-splits), `the_check`) — and in process `stand_mcp_tools` (blitz-tests; the flow through `serve_mcp` in both layout modes, one `tool_call` span the parent of each `command`; since 2026-10-19-visual-lint a `lint` tool call answering the reader's findings and parenting its `command` span; since 2026-11-07-ui-graph a `graph` tool call answering the reader's graph, its `tool_call` span parenting one `command` span that records `verb` alone, and since 2026-11-08-what-can-i-do-here an `actions` tool call answering the reader's nodes the same way, the two through one shared helper; since 2026-10-12-self-description every cause a tool call reaches served with its remedy, `covered` on an overlay fixture, and `help` answered by the server, parenting no `command` span) and, since 2026-10-12-self-description, `stand_mcp_masked` (a password typed through an MCP `type` reads `MASKED_VALUE` and never the typed text, role `PasswordInput` with 